# Minit — environment variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the real values.
# .env.local is git-ignored and must NEVER be committed (CLAUDE.md Hard Rule 4).

# --- AI: keys ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini API key (server-side only) — from https://aistudio.google.com
# ⚠ FREE TIER = Google's own pricing page says "Used to improve our products:
#   Yes". SAMPLE/FICTIONAL DATA ONLY until a PAID key is in use (PDPA — and
#   temple donor lists are probably SENSITIVE personal data: legal/PDPA-合规说明.md).
GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...

# OpenAI API key (server-side only) — from https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# Only needed if any AI_MODEL_* below points at "openai:".
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-...
# How much of the image the model sees: low | high | original | auto.
# Default "high". ⚠ On GPT-5.6, "auto"/"original" does NOT resize — a 3000x4000
# phone photo becomes ~11,750 patches of input. Leave this alone unless you have
# measured it. (src/lib/ai/openai.ts explains why.)
# OPENAI_IMAGE_DETAIL=high

# --- AI: which model does which job ------------------------------------------
# Format: provider:model   (provider must be exactly `gemini` or `openai`)
#
# Minit does four jobs of very different difficulty. Setting these four lines is
# what turns "planned per-task routing" into "shipped": the code has done this
# since 2026-08-03 (src/lib/ai/provider.ts resolveModel + every route already
# passes its task name), so THE ONLY THING MISSING IS THIS CONFIG. No code
# change is involved. Leave them unset and all four jobs fall back to
# AI_PROVIDER/GEMINI_MODEL below — i.e. one model for everything.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS COMMERCIALLY (npm run economics):
#   A · one model for everything, gemini-3.5-flash ........ 27.1% gross margin
#   B · one model for everything, claude-sonnet-5 ......... -16.5%  (loses money)
#   C · routing that also moves EXTRACT to OpenAI ......... 75.4%  ← DO NOT QUOTE
#   D · Gemini key only, flash-lite everywhere ............ 66.6%  ← reachable TODAY
#   E · routing that leaves EXTRACT on measured Gemini .... 73.4%  ← what we quote
#
# C and E differ by one line, and that line is the whole argument. C routes the
# handwriting to gpt-5.6-luna, a model that has never been through our eval, so
# its two extra points of margin rest on an accuracy assumption nobody checked.
# On 2026-08-05 the published figure was moved from C to E for that reason.
# Do not quietly move it back for the two points.
#
# After editing this file's real counterpart (.env.local), run:
#     npm run check:ai
# It reports what each task ACTUALLY resolves to via the app's own
# resolveModel(), so a silently-ignored line cannot go unnoticed.
# Classification + chat are 83% of call volume and need none of the capability
# that reads handwriting. Routing is a commercial requirement, not an optimisation.
#
# ⚠ Do NOT change AI_MODEL_EXTRACT on price alone. That is the handwriting job,
#   and accuracy IS the product. Run `npm run eval` first. Full runbook:
#   docs/换模型手册.md
#
# ⚠ THREE TRAPS, all verified against src/lib/ai/provider.ts:
#   1. A value with NO colon is SILENTLY IGNORED (provider.ts:122 only parses a
#      value containing ":"). `AI_MODEL_CHAT=gpt-5-nano` does not error — it
#      quietly falls back to Gemini and you think routing is on when it is not.
#   2. A value WITH a colon but an unknown provider THROWS at request time.
#      Only `gemini` and `openai` are accepted.
#   3. The model name itself is NOT validated. A typo passes startup and fails
#      at the vendor call, and an unpriced model makes cost tracking return null
#      instead of wrong (gemini.ts / openai.ts price tables) — honest, but you
#      lose the cost row you were trying to collect.

# --- OPTION E (what we quote: 73.4%) — NEEDS AN OPENAI KEY, which does not
#     exist yet. This is SCENARIO_ROUTED_SAFE in src/lib/unit-economics.ts.
#     Cheap models take classification and chat; the handwriting stays on the
#     Gemini model our eval actually measured.
# AI_MODEL_CLASSIFY=openai:gpt-5-nano            # ✅ "notes or ledger?" — trivial, 100 of 481 calls
# AI_MODEL_EXTRACT=gemini:gemini-3.5-flash-lite  # ✅ THE HARD ONE — deliberately NOT OpenAI
# AI_MODEL_CHAT=openai:gpt-5-nano                # ✅ short text Q&A, 250 of 481 calls
# AI_MODEL_LONG_DOC=gemini:gemini-3.5-flash-lite # ✅ 30-page constitutions

# --- OPTION C (75.4%) — the same thing with EXTRACT moved to OpenAI too.
#     Left here only so nobody re-derives it and thinks it is an upgrade.
#     ⛔ Do not use without running `npm run eval` on gpt-5.6-luna first.
# AI_MODEL_EXTRACT=openai:gpt-5.6-luna
# AI_MODEL_LONG_DOC=openai:gpt-5.6-luna

# --- OPTION D (reachable today with only GEMINI_API_KEY: 66.6%) -------------
#     All four Gemini, because flash-lite is the cheapest Gemini vision model
#     we have priced — so on one vendor "routing" collapses to one model. Still
#     worth setting explicitly: it pins the model instead of inheriting a
#     default that may change under you.
# AI_MODEL_CLASSIFY=gemini:gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# AI_MODEL_EXTRACT=gemini:gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# AI_MODEL_CHAT=gemini:gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# AI_MODEL_LONG_DOC=gemini:gemini-3.5-flash-lite
#
# Model names with a known price (anything else = costMicros null):
#   gemini: gemini-3.1-flash-lite, gemini-3.5-flash-lite, gemini-3-flash,
#           gemini-3.5-flash, gemini-3.6-flash            (src/lib/ai/gemini.ts)
#   openai: gpt-5-nano, gpt-5-mini, gpt-5.4-nano, gpt-5.4-mini, gpt-5.6-luna,
#           gpt-5.6-terra, gpt-5.6-sol, gpt-4.1-nano, gpt-4.1-mini
#                                                        (src/lib/ai/openai.ts)
# ⚠ Prices checked 2026-08-03. Vendors retire models — verify before quoting.

# --- AI: legacy fallback (still honoured, used when the four above are unset)
AI_PROVIDER=gemini
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna

# Supabase project URL — Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Supabase SERVICE ROLE key (server-side only, bypasses RLS — keep secret!)
# Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API > service_role
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...

# --- Phase 7 (auth) — PUBLIC values, safe for the browser -------------------
# Same project URL as SUPABASE_URL, but exposed to the browser for login.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# The PUBLIC "anon" key (NOT service_role!) — safe because row-level security
# decides what each logged-in user can see.
# Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API > anon public
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...
